# Added 2026-10-27 (Trivy DB of that day): gosu 1.19 is built with Go 1.24.6 (crypto/x509, fixed in
# Go 1.26.10 / 1.27.3). gosu 1.20 (2026-10-25) is not yet in any official postgres:18 (trixie, bookworm,
# alpine) or mongo:8.0 image, so no newer clean tag exists; gosu opens no TLS connection and verifies no certificate.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-23

# js-yaml in the Node.js tools bundled with mongo:8.0 (mongosh); the stack does not run mongosh.
# Upstream must update it.
CVE-2026-59869 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-84375 exp:2026-11-23
GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj exp:2026-11-23

# Go standard library (crypto/x509, certificate chains with untrusted intermediates) in gosu of
# postgres:18-alpine and mongo:8.0 and in the caddy binary of caddy:2.11-alpine, the newest tags
# on 2026-10-27; the fix needs a rebuild with Go 1.26.10. gosu opens no network connection, and
# the local proxy serves plain HTTP and verifies no client or upstream certificate (TLS comes
# with R14). Upstream must rebuild the images.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-23

# brotli decoder (brotli-libs, libbrotli1) and curl/libcurl (HTTP/2 upload) in postgres:18-alpine,
# couchdb:3.5, and caddy:2.11-alpine: the fixed Alpine and Debian packages came out after the
# newest tags were built (2026-10-21 to 2026-10-26). The libraries are only pulled in by curl;
# the stack runs locally, its health checks use curl only against 127.0.0.1, and no service
# uploads over HTTP/2 or decodes brotli data from outside. Upstream must rebuild the images.
CVE-2026-111497 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-92392 exp:2026-11-23

# Jackson and Jetty in the Nouveau search server bundled with couchdb:3.5 (opt/couchdb/nouveau);
# 3.5.3 of 2026-10-21 is the newest release and still ships them. CouchDB does not start Nouveau
# (it is off by default, and the stack neither enables nor runs it), so the Java code is never
# executed. Upstream must update the bundled libraries.
CVE-2026-68494 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-89407 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-89425 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-54512 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-54513 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-68497 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-91776 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-91777 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-2332 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-10050 exp:2026-11-23
# Added 2026-10-28: Guava (denial of service) in the same Nouveau server; fixed in Guava 33.7.2.
CVE-2026-102554 exp:2026-11-23

# go-jose v4.1.5 (denial of service when parsing JWKs with RSA keys) in the weed binary of
# chrislusf/seaweedfs:4.51 and the caddy binary of caddy:2.11-alpine, found on 2026-10-28; fixed
# in go-jose 4.1.6. Both services listen only on 127.0.0.1 in the local stack and parse no JWKs
# from outside. Upstream must rebuild the images.
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2026-11-23

# Added 2026-11-03 (observability profile, #82): OpenSSL (libcrypto3, libssl3) 3.5.6 in node:24.14-alpine
# (Alpine 3.23.4), which only runs the configuration step of the observability stack. The fix is
# OpenSSL 3.5.8-r0; no node image has it yet (checked: 24.14-alpine, 24.14-alpine3.23, 24.22-alpine on
# 2026-11-03, the newer one has other findings in npm). The step opens no network connection and no
# TLS connection. Upstream must rebuild the image.
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-11-23
CVE-2026-45447 exp:2026-11-23

